---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactInfo from '../../components/ContactInfo.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Do Code That Matters"
  description="Spencer Kittleson - Software engineer, maker, and technology enthusiast."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-2xl">
    <style>
      @keyframes wave {
        0% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
        20% { transform: rotate(-10deg); }
        40% { transform: rotate(10deg); }
        60% { transform: rotate(-10deg); }
        80% { transform: rotate(10deg); }
        100% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
      }
      .wave {
        animation: wave 2s infinite;
        font-size: 2rem;
        display: inline-block;
      }
    </style>

    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">
      Hi, I'm <strong>Spencer</strong> <span class="wave">👋</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="mb-4 text-[#a0aec0] font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
      I like to make things work... in software, on the bench, and around the house.
      I'm a software engineer who spends most of my days building and scaling systems
      with a focus on .NET, authentication, and database design. When the compiler
      stops yelling at me, I'm usually 3D printing something, wiring up a Raspberry Pi,
      or automating another part of the house.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-6 text-[#a0aec0] font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
      This site is where I write down what i build and what i learn along the way.
      The name says it: do code that matters. Build something real, ship it, and make
      sure it helps someone.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Things i've built</h2>

    <ul class="mb-6 space-y-3 text-[#a0aec0] font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        <span class="text-[#f5f5f5]">OAuth / SSO.</span>{' '}
        Worked through token exchange and SSO flows end to end.{' '}
        <a href="/blog/oauth-token-exchange-sso-demo/" class="text-[#9da2ff] hover:underline">Read the writeup</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-[#f5f5f5]">Rust + mixed-OS tooling.</span>{' '}
        Built a custom HTTP proxy in Rust to get corporate VPN working on Linux.{' '}
        <a href="/blog/building-custom-http-proxy-rust-mixed-os-workflows/" class="text-[#9da2ff] hover:underline">Read the writeup</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-[#f5f5f5]">Home automation.</span>{' '}
        Sprinklers, sensors, and smart switches that run local first.{' '}
        <a href="/blog/small-home-automations/" class="text-[#9da2ff] hover:underline">Small automations</a>
        {' '}&{' '}
        <a href="/blog/automate-sprinkler-with-tasmota/" class="text-[#9da2ff] hover:underline">the sprinkler build</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="text-[#f5f5f5]">Hardware that ships.</span>{' '}
        A DIY electric skateboard with a 3D printed parametric gear.{' '}
        <a href="/blog/diy-electric-skateboard/" class="text-[#9da2ff] hover:underline">Read the writeup</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">How i got here</h2>

    <p class="mb-6 text-[#a0aec0] font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
      I started out wanting to understand how things worked, and the only way to find
      out was to take them apart. That turned into a career building software for a
      living, and a habit of building stuff for fun that never really went away. The
      line between the two got blurry fast... a camera hack needs Python and OpenCV, a
      sprinkler needs MQTT and Grafana, and a proxy needs Rust. i dont separate them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">What im after</h2>

    <p class="mb-6 text-[#a0aec0] font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed">
      My goal is simple: build software that's efficient, reliable, and a joy for other
      developers to use. Then write down what i learned so it helps someone else. If
      you're reading this, you're probably one of those someones.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-6 text-[#f5f5f5] font-mono text-sm">Interested in consulting?</p>

    <ContactInfo />

    <hr class="my-8 border-white/10" />

    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-6">Contact Me</h2>

    <form
      id="messageForm"
      class="max-w-lg space-y-4"
      onsubmit="event.preventDefault(); fetchContactRelay(this);"
    >
      <div>
        <label for="emailFormControlInput" class="block text-sm font-mono text-[#a0aec0] mb-1">
          Email address
        </label>
        <input
          type="email"
          id="emailFormControlInput"
          placeholder="name@example.com"
          required
          class="w-full bg-[#1a2129] border border-white/20 rounded px-3 py-2 text-sm font-mono text-[#f5f5f5] placeholder-[#a0aec0] focus:outline-none focus:border-[#9da2ff]"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label for="messageFormControlInput" class="block text-sm font-mono text-[#a0aec0] mb-1">
          Message
        </label>
        <textarea
          id="messageFormControlInput"
          rows="6"
          minlength="10"
          required
          class="w-full bg-[#1a2129] border border-white/20 rounded px-3 py-2 text-sm font-mono text-[#f5f5f5] placeholder-[#a0aec0] focus:outline-none focus:border-[#9da2ff] resize-y"
        ></textarea>
      </div>
      <div>
        <input
          id="submitFormControlInput"
          type="submit"
          value="Send"
          class="bg-[#9da2ff] text-[#232b32] font-mono text-sm px-6 py-2 rounded cursor-pointer hover:bg-[#b8bcff] transition-colors disabled:opacity-50 disabled:cursor-not-allowed"
        />
      </div>
    </form>

    <div id="contactThankYou" class="hidden max-w-lg" role="status">
      <p class="font-mono text-sm font-bold mb-1" style="color: var(--color-accent);">
        &check; Message sent
      </p>
      <p class="font-mono text-sm text-[#a0aec0]">
        Thanks for reaching out... i'll get back to you soon.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div id="contactError" class="hidden max-w-lg mt-3" role="alert">
      <p class="font-mono text-sm" style="color: #f87171;">
        <span id="contactErrorDetail">Something went wrong sending your message.</span>
        Please try again.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script src="/site.js" defer></script>
  <script src="/contact-relay.js" defer></script>
</BaseLayout>
